Let's put our fate within
this light under the sun.

81
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:28,937
Can you close your eyes and
just listen to my voice.

82
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:32,597
Let's find the answer
together, I'm telling you.

83
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,737
In our path I trust that it will lead us.

84
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:39,457
To another sea untarded,
cause now we are home.

85
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:42,337
On the horizon, out on
the edge of the world.

86
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:45,277
There is a place that I wanna take you to.

87
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:48,117
Let's head forward then,
but ask for the way.

88
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,340
We already know.

89
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:53,500
We promised it long ago.

90
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:06,060
Are you still trying to stand?

91
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,500
I am.

92
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:13,020
Why hurt yourself?

93
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:16,381
You must really want another
thrashing, don't you?

94
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:21,600
You want that stone so badly, huh?

95
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,040
You're not trying to rescue Sanji,

96
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:28,200
leaving him and focusing on the
polyglyph instead. That's right.

97
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:34,577
There's one thing about
Sanji; he's kind to a fault,

98
00:08:34,660 --> 00:08:39,717
so I thought right from the start
that he might not be returning to our

99
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:44,657
crew—that isn't to say I've figured out
exactly what trap you've set for him.

100
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:49,057
But knowing Sanji's considerate nature,

101
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:53,057
if he's made up his mind to
sacrifice himself for someone,

102
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:54,497
then he will not back down.

103
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:58,557
Our captain on the other
hand will follow his

104
