also, please notify the vinsmokes.

254
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:28,037
Surely they'll be worried, sir?

255
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:31,640
Well, I'll be at the medical
center on the fourth floor.

256
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:36,337
After all, there's plenty of wounded
soldiers in the Shit tonight.

257
00:18:36,420 --> 00:18:38,997
I doubt I'll be able to
find the time to sleep,

258
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,315
thank you for your service, take care.

259
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:02,140
Where am I?

260
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,010
Sanji!

261
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:13,080
I hurt my leg.

262
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:17,182
Do you recall how you got
hurt, or what happened?

263
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:22,260
I remember walking around the castle,

264
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:26,639
and then came across some soldiers
who were shouting about intruders.

265
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,440
I must have gotten involved somehow.

266
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:31,857
Reizhu, think harder.

267
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:33,020
That's not it.

268
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,560
Your memories were overwritten.

269
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:37,700
I'll fill you in.

270
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,220
But let me warn you,
the truth is damn ugly.

271
00:19:46,900 --> 00:19:49,800
These books are susceptible to fire!

272
00:19:50,260 --> 00:19:53,500
Wait, you're going to torch
the cage with us inside?

273
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:56,857
Just leave the enclosure before
you're engulfed in flames.

274
00:19:56,940 --> 00:20:00,860
It's really quite simple.
Do it then! Go! That quick?

275
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:03,220
Wait, I'm not on board yet!

276
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:07,760
Oh, we're gonna get incinerated!

277
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:09,760
Burn faster!

278
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:20,200
Burn! Lupus! Coming!

279
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:37,760
We're free now!

280
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:42,980
Damn it.

281
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:47,085
Why do I feel like I've been
through something like this before?

282
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:49,060
You survived. Well done.

283
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:53,977
Because of you, I didn't
have to rip my hands off.

284
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:54,890
So thanks.

285
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,059
It just struck me.

286
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:59,062
Do you remember the first
time we met each other?

287
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:02,420
Coincidentally, it was also in a prison.

288
00:21:02,620 --> 00:21:04,837
And look, that very same cage.

289
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:07,820
also held all these
prisoners within its pages.

290
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:11,880
The world of books is as
infinite as your own imagination.

291
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:17,320
Do take note that Big Mom's allies
and lackeys are quite formidable.

292
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:24,180
Thanks a bunch, Chimbe.

293
00:21:24,760 --> 00:21:27,540
So, what are you doing here? Well,

294
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,260
it's a bit complicated,

295
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:34,342
but as Captain of the Sun Pirates, I have
an affiliation with Big Mom and her crew.

296
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:35,750
Do you really?

297
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:40,160
Then what about all this?

298
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:43,480
I suppose you'd call it a rebellion.

299
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:45,320
No turning back now.

300
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:48,360
You're laughing?

301
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,337
But what about your responsibilities?

302
00:21:50,420 --> 00:21:51,655
Wasn't that an issue?

303
00:21:51,940 --> 00:21:53,760
I have cast them aside.

304
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:56,552
The screams came from the prison library.

305
00:21:57,180 --> 00:21:58,920
What's going on? Great.

306
00:21:59,080 --> 00:22:00,139
They already know.

307
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,162
Not surprising.

308
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,150
They're quick.

309
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:04,680
We must find a place to conceal ourselves.

310
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:07,440
Hurry, they draw close. Good call.

311
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:08,980
Here, follow me.

312
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,380
So we can't move.

313
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:14,660
Too hungry.

314
00:22:15,020 --> 00:22:18,000
At a time like this? Truly? Oh, right.

315
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:19,280
Luffy burns out.

316
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:22,382
He expends energy three
times faster than others.

317
00:22:22,660 --> 00:22:23,490
Don't worry.

318
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:26,700
I didn't say I needed to eat. I'm fine.

319
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,740
Luffy, your stomach speaks.

320
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:33,140
Ignore it.

321
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:35,340
Hey, Sanji!

322
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:38,960
I won't eat anything unless you cook it!

323
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:41,080
Even if I get hungry,

324
00:22:41,340 --> 00:22:47,400
even if spears or swords or stones rain
down on me, I'll keep waiting for you!

325
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:50,900
Anyway, Jinbei, thank you.

326
00:22:55,360 --> 00:23:01,197
The, uh, truth is, I met with
Sanji, and he proposed to me.

327
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:06,017
The reason why we're not
getting married is because

328
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:09,260
that love-born fool played
right into my hands.

329
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:14,880
And during the wedding ceremony, I
planned to shoot him full of holes.

330
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,760
Things are pretty bad as is.

331
00:23:17,960 --> 00:23:20,560
We were all tricked by
them, Sanji included.

332
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:22,160
I need to warn him!

333
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,740
Look after Nami, Jinbei!

334
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:26,860
Just a word of caution.

335
00:23:27,180 --> 00:23:28,977
There are many guards outside!

336
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:32,420
Also, you're not fully
recovered. Be careful.

337
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:34,497
You went through a lot this morning.

338
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:36,180
I'll be fine. I promise.

339
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,700
Think I'm lying?

340
00:23:58,300 --> 00:23:59,260
I don't.

341
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:01,557
I know you would never mislead me.

342
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:05,357
I was wary of Pudding, but didn't
imagine her to be this devious.

343
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,077
I had my suspicions.

344
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:12,760
She just seemed a little too perfect for
me, so I thought I should eavesdrop a bit.

345
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:15,160
I really screwed up.

346
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:20,260
I assumed if I accepted the marriage,
they would spare my crewmates.

347
00:24:21,580 --> 00:24:24,177
It turns out that was never in the cards.

348
00:24:24,260 --> 00:24:25,780
It was all a ploy.

349
00:24:26,080 --> 00:24:28,198
Of course they were blowing smoke up

350
00:24:29,260 --> 00:24:30,090
my ass.

351
00:24:30,173 --> 00:24:32,897
I thought everything would work
out if I took one for the team.

352
00:24:32,980 --> 00:24:34,660
What kind of a fantasy was

353
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:37,670
I living in?

354
00:24:37,753 --> 00:24:38,997
I should have known better.

355
00:24:39,080 --> 00:24:40,920
They fooled our father, too.

356
00:24:41,160 --> 00:24:43,817
He's a wise man, But he was
undone by his arrogance.

357
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:48,237
He's dealing with an emperor; he
should have been more cautious.

358
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:52,957
And now it's far too late—this
still might play out for the best,

359
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:57,117
though I believe that
Germa should be destroyed.

360
00:24:57,200 --> 00:25:00,637
I'd like to pretend I'm ignorant

361
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:04,277
and let Big Mom carry out her plan.

362
00:25:04,360 --> 00:25:05,317
Don't be stupid!

363
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:08,420
stupid They'll kill
you tomorrow too, Race!

364
00:25:09,640 --> 00:25:12,840
Aw, is my little brother concerned for me?

365
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:19,524
Leave the past where it
lies, where beyond that.

366
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,797
You don't owe me a single thing.

367
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:23,645
I only helped you once before.

368
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:29,300
Go find the Straw Hats and leave
this island, Sanji. Like how?

369
00:25:29,460 --> 00:25:30,520
I can't do that!

370
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:33,137
What do you think would
happen to the Baratier?

371
00:25:33,220 --> 00:25:34,050
Just run.

372
00:25:34,133 --> 00:25:36,296
Figure that out after you've escaped.

373
00:25:36,620 --> 00:25:38,620
Stay here and all of you will die.

374
00:25:39,240 --> 00:25:42,760
Sanji, you have to live
for our mother's sake.

375
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:44,640
Why bring her up?

376
00:25:45,900 --> 00:25:49,120
Because there's one memory I can't forget.

377
00:25:57,320 --> 00:25:58,580
What do you mean?

378
00:25:59,200 --> 00:26:00,440
What memory?

379
00:26:01,040 --> 00:26:03,197
There was a fight between our parents.

380
00:26:03,280 --> 00:26:05,880
I was just a child at the time,

381
00:26:06,120 --> 00:26:08,457
so I didn't understand the catalyst of our

382
00:26:08,540 --> 00:26:11,305
mother's resentment of
father until much later.

383
00:26:11,620 --> 00:26:13,444
But it's obvious in retrospect.

384
00:26:15,940 --> 00:26:18,777
While our mother was still
carrying the four of you,

385
00:26:18,860 --> 00:26:20,877
she was quite adamant against turning you

386
00:26:20,960 --> 00:26:23,725
quadruplets into cold-blooded
killing machines.

387
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:27,297
You're not serious!

388
00:26:27,380 --> 00:26:28,760
Of course I am. Never!

389
00:26:29,140 --> 00:26:30,905
How could you do that to them?

390
00:26:31,980 --> 00:26:32,810
Enough.

391
00:26:32,893 --> 00:26:34,237
The surgery is already arranged.

392
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:35,240
Don't do this!

393
00:26:35,380 --> 00:26:37,145
These are my children as well!

394
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:39,300
I beg you! Please, Judge!

395
00:26:39,500 --> 00:26:40,971
They need their humanity!

396
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:42,820
Being human won't cut it.

397
00:26:43,080 --> 00:26:45,000
Not when monsters win wars.

398
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:49,197
Our end goal is to reclaim the North Blue

399
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:52,020
by force and restore
it to its former glory.

400
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:55,877
Accomplishing that vision
will take incredible strength,

401
00:26:55,960 --> 00:27:00,020
which is the reason I give
this gift to my own progeny!

402
00:27:00,860 --> 00:27:02,680
Stop take her away

403
00:27:10,220 --> 00:27:12,360
They forced the surgery on her

404
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:22,480
But our mother took a toxin attempting
to foil our father's plan he was furious

405
00:27:38,760 --> 00:27:44,717
no what did you just do it was a
powerful drug strong enough to affect

406
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:51,560
the manipulated bloodline elements
unfortunately it wasn't enough

407
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:56,757
it didn't take long before superhuman like

408
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:59,546
abnormalities began
appearing in our brother's

409
00:28:05,080 --> 00:28:09,857
Bodies the operation was a great success
wonderful I'm delighted to report

410
00:28:09,940 --> 00:28:14,411
that their genetic blueprints were not
altered in any which way by the toxin

411
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:29,697
you wanna play master sanji on
the other hand is trailing behind

412
00:28:29,780 --> 00:28:34,440
we'll monitor the boy perhaps
his development is a bit delayed

413
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:51,740
You two must be hungry.

414
00:28:52,100 --> 00:28:53,100
Just one second.

415
00:28:54,080 --> 00:28:55,000
Here.

416
00:28:56,340 --> 00:28:57,640
Is it good?

417
00:28:58,500 --> 00:28:59,330
Whoa!

418
00:29:00,080 --> 00:29:02,657
Master Sanji is feeding animals.

419
00:29:02,740 --> 00:29:06,600
He was supposed to be
devoid of emotions! Saru!

420
00:29:07,540 --> 00:29:10,420
You were growing, but
not as father wanted.

421
00:29:10,740 --> 00:29:11,858
You had compassion.

422
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:13,750
Meanwhile,

423
00:29:13,833 --> 00:29:18,482
our mother got weaker and weaker due to
the long-term effects caused by the poison.

424
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:24,100
She died because of me, then?
Nonsense. Don't think that way.

425
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,920
Mother? Reiju!

426
00:29:29,300 --> 00:29:30,320
Hello, dear.

427
00:29:32,220 --> 00:29:33,997
How's your father treating you?

428
00:29:34,080 --> 00:29:37,917
The only thing that he wants
to do is make us train.

429
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,237
It's dumb.

430
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:43,520
He's only happy when Ichiji,
Niji and Yonji get stronger.

431
00:29:45,540 --> 00:29:47,897
I see what's that?

432
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:49,357
Take a look.

433
00:29:49,440 --> 00:29:52,157
Sanji cooked me a meal all by himself!

434
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:54,060
Wow really.

435
00:29:57,200 --> 00:30:01,640
Guess what Sanji told me
today that boy. It's so sweet

436
00:30:03,980 --> 00:30:06,000
He said, get better.

437
00:30:08,820 --> 00:30:10,740
He's the best son ever.

438
00:30:14,220 --> 00:30:16,260
What are you doing here?

439
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:18,700
Uh, Dad...

440
00:30:22,460 --> 00:30:25,200
Flowers for the dead is a pointless rite.

441
00:30:25,420 --> 00:30:27,302
You're proving your uselessness.

442
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:42,200
Stop your crying!

443
00:30:46,080 --> 00:30:46,910
What?!

444
00:30:46,993 --> 00:30:47,840
Coward!

445
00:30:52,340 --> 00:30:53,500
Let's go.

446
00:30:55,100 --> 00:30:56,720
You too, Reiju.

447
00:30:58,300 --> 00:30:59,130
Sir.

448
00:31:03,200 --> 00:31:06,847
Our father's beliefs were
completely contrary to our mother's.

449
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:09,760
That's why he could never
accept who you were.

450
00:31:13,800 --> 00:31:16,329
He blamed you for
everything that happened.

451
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:18,579
He lashed out at you as punishment.

452
00:31:20,240 --> 00:31:21,070
There!

453
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:22,700
Don't ever cook again!

454
00:31:23,240 --> 00:31:24,300
I'm pulling back!

455
00:31:24,700 --> 00:31:25,540
Attack me!

456
00:31:29,580 --> 00:31:32,400
How is Sanji such a worthless failure?

457
00:31:33,080 --> 00:31:34,840
Failure! Failure!

458
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:47,360
Now go!

459
00:31:48,940 --> 00:31:50,960
And don't look back!

460
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:54,140
Even though Mother has passed,

461
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:56,200
she's still here.

462
00:31:56,700 --> 00:31:58,406
Her kindness lives on in you.

463
00:31:59,300 --> 00:32:00,241
Needless to say,

464
00:32:00,740 --> 00:32:02,020
you are no failure.

465
00:32:02,840 --> 00:32:06,677
Just remember, our Mother
selflessly gave her life.

466
00:32:06,760 --> 00:32:09,020
to protect you and your humanity.

467
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:13,220
You are the future Mother wanted to see.

468
00:32:14,420 --> 00:32:19,040
That's why you're kinder
and more tender than anyone.

469
00:32:24,540 --> 00:32:26,140
Find Straw Hat!

470
00:32:26,760 --> 00:32:28,220
Which way did he go?

471
00:32:28,500 --> 00:32:32,437
He escaped the underground prison library
and passed through the first floor!

472
00:32:32,520 --> 00:32:33,350
Hurry up!

473
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,911
Head to the second floor!

474
00:32:35,320 --> 00:32:36,150
Sir!

475
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:40,750
Sochi!

476
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:45,832
What do you mean there's another problem?

477
00:32:46,240 --> 00:32:50,320
Well, there are reports that Boss
Jinbei's in the castle. Seriously?

478
00:32:50,640 --> 00:32:51,522
He's rebelling?

479
00:32:51,840 --> 00:32:53,500
Yes, it seems so.

480
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:55,110
All right.

481
00:32:55,193 --> 00:32:57,680
Send this message to
the troops. Yes, ma 'am.

482
00:33:02,700 --> 00:33:03,935
Tomorrow's a big day.

483
00:33:04,220 --> 00:33:05,457
Don't disappoint Mama.

484
00:33:05,540 --> 00:33:06,370
Of course not.

485
00:33:06,500 --> 00:33:08,853
Do you know what will happen if we fail?

486
00:33:09,020 --> 00:33:11,020
I asked a simple question.

487
00:33:11,540 --> 00:33:12,540
What'll happen?

488
00:33:20,900 --> 00:33:23,600
I don't even want to think about it.

489
00:33:23,860 --> 00:33:25,120
Now you understand.

490
00:33:25,860 --> 00:33:30,037
Considering that lesser inconveniences
have sent Mama into one of her mood swings,

491
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:32,532
we can't risk sabotaging tomorrow's plan.

492
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:34,200
Of course not.

493
00:33:34,660 --> 00:33:36,895
But there's an easy way to avoid that.

494
00:33:38,060 --> 00:33:40,620
You think we should lie?

495
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:44,104
If you lie to Mama, then
you'll be put to death.

496
00:33:44,700 --> 00:33:46,100
Please forgive me.

497
00:33:46,420 --> 00:33:48,817
You see, we don't need
to tell her anything.

498
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:50,500
If there is no problem.

499
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:52,732
You get what I'm saying?

500
00:33:53,260 --> 00:33:55,000
Yes, I do, ma 'am.

501
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:58,769
We're on the fourth floor.

502
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:01,341
Block off all paths leading here.

503
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:04,972
Then make sure everything on
the lower levels is in order.

504
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:07,517
Get a move on it and
take care of the problem.

505
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:09,160
Yes, ma 'am. Understood.

506
00:34:09,980 --> 00:34:10,880
But wait.

507
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:15,380
If we're in a hurry, it might be
faster just to kill them. Do whatever.

508
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,113
You have my permission.

509
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:18,510
Ma 'am!

510
00:34:18,720 --> 00:34:20,020
Spit it out!

511
00:34:20,240 --> 00:34:21,200
Where's Saint?

512
00:34:21,900 --> 00:34:22,730
Saint!

513
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,400
I know he's here!

514
00:34:29,580 --> 00:34:30,620
Just kill me!

515
00:34:33,640 --> 00:34:36,717
What is there to think about, you know?

516
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:38,800
In your heart, what you should do.

517
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:44,617
Just abandon Germa and flee to safety—it
represents nothing but destruction.

518
00:34:44,700 --> 00:34:49,657
Clinging to the glories of the past, the
world would be better off without us.

519
00:34:49,740 --> 00:34:50,570
All

520
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:53,077
big mom wants is our military technology.

521
00:34:53,160 --> 00:34:53,990
I

522
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:58,137
highly doubt she's interested
in taking your mentor's life.

523
00:34:58,220 --> 00:34:59,050
After

524
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:03,737
the wedding tomorrow, our father
and brothers will all be dead.

525
00:35:03,820 --> 00:35:04,650
dead Remember?

526
00:35:05,100 --> 00:35:07,747
So it's fine They can't
carry out the threat.

527
00:35:08,740 --> 00:35:09,857
Glorified murderers.

528
00:35:09,940 --> 00:35:12,560
That's what our family has always been.

529
00:35:13,180 --> 00:35:16,097
You know I can't stand all
those pretentious jerks!

530
00:35:16,180 --> 00:35:18,640
But why do you have to die, Reizhu?

531
00:35:19,220 --> 00:35:21,497
I still have my emotions intact.

532
00:35:21,580 --> 00:35:25,580
But father augmented me, so
I am unable to disobey him.

533
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:27,617
There's no way out, Sanji!

534
00:35:27,700 --> 00:35:29,940
But I have blood on my hands.

535
00:35:31,060 --> 00:35:32,001
I deserve death.

536
00:35:34,780 --> 00:35:37,560
Oh, by the way, those bracelets on you?

537
00:35:39,240 --> 00:35:41,500
I promise that they won't explode.

538
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:44,140
I swap them out for normal ones.

539
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:49,088
What other reason could
be keeping you here?

540
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:50,430
Honestly.

541
00:35:52,080 --> 00:35:53,668
Would you pull it together?

542
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:54,860
Wake up!

543
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:04,348
You need to think about
what really matters.

544
00:36:05,200 --> 00:36:06,700
Wish it was that simple.

545
00:36:07,660 --> 00:36:08,980
Stop, straw hands!

546
00:36:16,360 --> 00:36:18,595
Excuse me, why don't you join my crew?

547
00:36:19,340 --> 00:36:21,634
I could use a cook like you on my ship.

548
00:36:22,580 --> 00:36:23,410
Nodgy!

549
00:36:26,780 --> 00:36:30,317
You're a good cook, and I need one,
obviously—we should be pirates together.

550
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:31,230
You

551
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:38,077
have wonderful friends, people like
that—only come once in a lifetime.

552
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:38,990
Move on!

553
00:36:41,540 --> 00:36:42,660
move on
